messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2025,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "Artificial intelligence surpasses human experts in most cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "Autonomous systems manage logistics, coding, and scientific research, causing mass unemployment in white-collar sectors and prompting universal basic income experiments."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global average temperature exceeds 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels permanently.",
      "detail": "The West Antarctic ice sheet enters irreversible collapse, committing the planet to multi-meter sea level rise over subsequent centuries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Commercial nuclear fusion power achieves net energy gain and enters mass production.",
      "detail": "Tokamak reactors power major cities by 2040, ending fossil fuel dominance in the energy sector and causing atmospheric CO2 to peak around 450 ppm."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "World population peaks at approximately 10.4 billion before entering long-term decline.",
      "detail": "Global fertility rates fall below replacement level in most regions; the median age rises to 45, straining pension and healthcare systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "First permanent human settlement is established on Mars.",
      "detail": "A consortium of nations and private companies builds a habitat for 50 inhabitants using local water ice for fuel and oxygen."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "A severe global pandemic, whether natural or engineered, kills between 5% and 20% of the world's population.",
      "detail": "The catastrophe triggers a permanent global health surveillance state, biodefense infrastructure, and strict regulation of dual-use biotechnology."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Brain-computer interfaces become widely available consumer products.",
      "detail": "Neural devices enable direct thought-to-text communication and memory augmentation, raising profound privacy, security, and inequality concerns."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Sea levels rise by 0.5 meters, displacing roughly 500 million people from coastal regions.",
      "detail": "Major cities like Miami, Shanghai, and Mumbai face chronic flooding, forcing hundreds of millions to migrate inland or invest in massive sea defenses."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Radical life extension therapies extend healthy human lifespan to 120 years in developed nations.",
      "detail": "Senolytics and gene editing eliminate most age-related diseases, making multi-century careers and delayed retirement the norm."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Asteroid mining begins in near-Earth orbit, providing unlimited platinum-group metals and water.",
      "detail": "Commodity prices crash as resources are extracted from space, ending most terrestrial mining and allowing Earth's biosphere to recover from extraction pressure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Stratospheric aerosol injection geoengineering is deployed at scale to cool the planet by approximately 1°C.",
      "detail": "The intervention stabilizes temperatures but disrupts monsoon patterns, causing regional conflicts over rainfall and agricultural yields."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Traditional nation-states cede significant sovereignty to supranational AI governance networks and corporate entities.",
      "detail": "Algorithmic systems manage global resource allocation, climate policy, and dispute resolution, while traditional borders become less relevant."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Post-quantum cryptography becomes the global standard after quantum computers break legacy encryption.",
      "detail": "Quantum computers with millions of logical qubits render RSA and ECC obsolete, forcing a worldwide transition to lattice-based cryptographic systems within a decade."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Self-replicating von Neumann probes are launched toward Alpha Centauri at 0.1c.",
      "detail": "The probes carry replicators and stored human genetic information or digital consciousness templates to seed colonies upon arrival."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Earth's population declines to roughly 3 billion due to urbanization and off-world migration.",
      "detail": "Former agricultural land returns to wilderness, allowing biodiversity to recover significantly across the planet."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "First extrasolar human colony is established around Proxima Centauri b.",
      "detail": "A generation ship or relativistic ark arrives after decades of travel, establishing a self-sustaining colony of 10,000 inhabitants."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "First artificial megastructure, such as a ringworld, is completed around a distant star.",
      "detail": "The structure provides habitable surface area equivalent to millions of Earths, powered entirely by its parent star."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Orbital habitats house approximately 1 billion humans.",
      "detail": "O'Neill cylinders and Stanford toruses in Earth orbit and Lagrange points provide Earth-like gravity, while the planet's surface becomes a heritage reserve."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Post-human intelligences, including digital uploads and AI, outnumber biological humans by 10 to 1.",
      "detail": "Legal rights are extended to non-biological entities, and the definition of 'humanity' expands to encompass diverse forms of consciousness."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "A Dyson swarm captures 5% of the Sun's output, marking the transition toward a Kardashev Type II civilization.",
      "detail": "Solar collectors orbiting the sun generate 5×10^24 watts, powering industry across the entire solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Consciousness uploading becomes routine, making biological death optional.",
      "detail": "Minds are routinely copied to digital substrates, allowing individuals to exist in multiple instances or migrate between robotic and virtual bodies."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Interstellar civilization spans 50 light-years with 1,000 inhabited worlds.",
      "detail": "Relativistic ships and laser communication networks link colonies, though travel times keep most worlds culturally isolated."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Mars is fully terraformed with a breathable atmosphere.",
      "detail": "Centuries of genetically engineered cyanobacteria and imported volatiles create a thick atmosphere, allowing humans to walk outdoors without suits."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "The Milky Way contains 100,000 human-descended civilizations.",
      "detail": "Relativistic expansion fills the galaxy, with diverse cultures, speciation events, and technological paths creating thousands of distinct societies."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Stellar engineering projects begin moving stars to prevent the Milky Way-Andromeda collision.",
      "detail": "Shkadov thrusters reposition sun-like stars into stable, long-lived configurations, extending the habitable lifespan of the galaxy by billions of years."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Computronium substrates dominate, housing the majority of intelligent minds.",
      "detail": "Planet-sized computers powered by stellar energy run vast simulations and minds, while biological humans exist only as a small, preserved minority in reserves."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Either contact with extraterrestrial intelligence occurs, or humanity is confirmed alone in the galaxy.",
      "detail": "Radio and optical surveys either detect alien signals, initiating a galactic exchange of knowledge, or confirm the Fermi paradox, shifting focus entirely inward."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Galactic civilization approaches Kardashev Type III, harnessing the energy of the entire Milky Way.",
      "detail": "Energy use reaches 10^37 watts by utilizing all 100-400 billion stars in the galaxy for computation and industry."
    },
    {
      "year": 9500,
      "event": "Matrioshka brains (nested Dyson spheres) are constructed around all major stars.",
      "detail": "These nested shells maximize computational capacity by using waste heat from inner layers to power outer layers, creating the ultimate computing substrate."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity exists as a galaxy-spanning post-biological civilization, or has gone extinct centuries earlier.",
      "detail": "If extant, trillions of minds inhabit millions of worlds across the Milky Way, unrecognizable as biological humans of 2025; if not, the silence of the galaxy remains."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity likely faces severe existential risks this century from pandemics, climate disruption, and unaligned AI, with a substantial probability of extinction before 2200. If it survives these bottlenecks and becomes multi-planetary, it will probably expand across the galaxy and evolve into post-biological forms, making survival to year 10000 plausible but by no means guaranteed."
}
